PART 3 — TOKEN LIFECYCLE & SCANNER

15. AUTOMATIC TOKEN REMOVAL

If a token is no longer valid for active analysis, Brigg must remove it from the active analysis list immediately or after a properly configured validation/stale-data threshold.

Possible conditions include:

- data feed becomes stale
- pair becomes invalid
- token no longer satisfies scanner criteria
- liquidity becomes invalid
- required market data disappears
- token is no longer available from the active data source

Do not remove a token merely because it has had a few seconds of low activity.

Use a proper stale-data/validation mechanism.

---

16. AUTOMATIC REPLACEMENT

When an active token is removed, the scanner should allow another qualifying token to enter the available analysis slot.

Example:

TOKEN A
Active
   ↓
Data becomes invalid
   ↓
Remove TOKEN A
   ↓
Scanner searches qualifying tokens
   ↓
TOKEN B enters

The scanner should continuously maintain the active analysis universe according to the configured criteria.

---

