20. EXAMPLE — OPPORTUNITY SCORE GUIDE

Example:

OPPORTUNITY SCORE
77/100

Explain:

What is it?

A composite measure describing how favorable the
current setup appears according to Brigg's configured
analysis.

The score may consider factors such as:

• Momentum
• Volume
• Liquidity
• Wallet activity
• Social activity
• Execution conditions
• Market regime

Then explain that a high Opportunity Score does not automatically mean BUY.

This distinction must be explicitly taught.

---

