---

FINAL ACCEPTANCE CRITERIA

The update is complete only when:

1. Existing Action State classifications remain unchanged.
2. "HIGH-RISK OPPORTUNITY", "WAIT", "NO TRADE", etc. are not replaced by BUY/SELL.
3. Live Signal is a separate optional feature.
4. User can turn Live Signal ON/OFF.
5. When OFF, the Terminal looks and behaves as before regarding Action State.
6. When ON, Live Signal can show BUY, HOLD, PARTIAL SELL, or SELL.
7. Live Signal updates from actual current market data.
8. Live Signal can be displayed on the chart.
9. Live Signal has confidence and explanation options.
10. Chart can expand to a large/fullscreen view.
11. Chart remains live after expansion.
12. Chart tools and objects are usable and manageable.
13. Invalid/stale tokens are removed according to validated lifecycle rules.
14. Replacement tokens can enter the scanner.
15. Terminal Guide exists inside Settings.
16. Terminal Guide contains illustrations and beginner explanations.
17. Short video tutorials can be added to the guide.
18. ML Help/Guide exists inside ML Center.
19. ML concepts are explained in both technical and beginner-friendly language.
20. ML Learning Activity displays actual system events.
21. User can switch between Technical and Explain-to-Me views.
22. Daily Learning Summary is available.
23. Existing validation gates remain intact.
24. Existing model promotion and rollback functionality remains intact.
25. No fabricated ML events, metrics, observations, or learning claims are introduced.
26. All new UI components are responsive and work on both desktop and mobile.
27. Existing Brigg functionality must not be broken or removed while implementing these updates.